Name: Firebase Analytics and aligned runtime dependencies
URL: https://firebase.google.com/docs/analytics
Version: Analytics 24.0.0 (Firebase BoM 35.0.2)
License: Android Software Development Kit License (Analytics/Measurement/ads-identifier); Apache-2.0 (Firebase core and Kotlin coroutines)
Security Critical: yes
Shipped: yes

Pinned from Google Maven and Maven Central. Exact URLs and SHA-256 hashes are
in artifacts.json; fetch.py restores or checks those artifacts.

Used only when lemurx_enable_firebase=true. Chromium already ships coroutines
1.11.0, so only kotlinx-coroutines-play-services is overridden (1.9.0 -> 1.11.0).
Firebase common 23.0.0, components 20.0.0, annotations 18.0.0, installations
20.0.0 and installations-interop 18.0.0 replace the older autorolled copies.
Measurement 24.0.0 and play-services-ads-identifier 18.0.0 are new targets;
this Chromium revision does not vendor them.

play-services-measurement-impl-24.0.0.aar is locally patched: zzwu no longer
calls Futures.propagateCancellation (absent from public Guava). It calls
org.chromium.chrome.browser.lemurx.firebase.GuavaFuturesCompat instead.
fetch.py --check expects the patched bytes.
